      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58561,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 231,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> myofibrosarcoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:24:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 399,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 232,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58562,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 232,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:24:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 400,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 233,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58563,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 233,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Low-grade myofibroblastic sarcoma shows a wide anatomical distribution; extremities and the head and neck region, especially the tongue and oral cavity, are preferred locations, whereas the skin and gastrointestinal tract are rarely affected {9777985; 11176071; 17513510; 27377169}. These neoplasms arise predominantly in subcutaneous and deeper soft tissues; dermal presentation is very uncommon {11510507}. Rare cases involving salivary gland and nasal cavity&nbsp;/ paranasal sinuses have been reported {10555016; 11493344}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:24:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 401,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 234,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58564,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 234,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most patients report a painless swelling or an enlarging mass. Pain or related symptoms have more rarely been reported. Radiologically, these lesions have a destructive growth pattern.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:24:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 402,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 235,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58565,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 235,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Low-grade myofibroblastic sarcoma occurs predominantly in adults, with a slight male predominance; children are more rarely affected {9777985; 11176071; 8597827}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:24:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 403,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 236,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58566,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 236,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:24:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 404,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 237,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58567,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 237,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:24:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 411,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 244,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58568,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 244,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Grossly, the tumour is usually a firm mass with pale, fibrous cut surfaces and ill-defined margins {9777985}; a minority are well circumscribed with pushing margins {11176071}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:24:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 405,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 238,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58569,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 238,
        "headingText": "<p>Histologically, low-grade myofibroblastic sarcomas are characterized by a diffusely infiltrative growth pattern, and (in deeply located neoplasms) tumour cells often grow between individual skeletal muscle fibres. Most cases are composed of spindle-shaped tumour cells arranged in cellular fascicles or show a storiform growth pattern. Neoplastic cells have ill-defined palely eosinophilic cytoplasm and fusiform nuclei that are either elongated and wavy with evenly distributed chromatin or plumper, more rounded, and vesicular with small nucleoli. Rarely, hypocellular neoplasms with a more prominent collagenous (sometimes hyalinized) stroma have been described. Importantly, neoplastic cells show, at least focally, moderate nuclear atypia with enlarged, hyperchromatic, and irregular nuclei and slightly increased proliferative activity. These neoplasms may contain numerous thin-walled capillaries. The tumours may progress to morphologically higher-grade myofibroblastic sarcomas {11176071}. By immunohistochemistry, neoplastic cells in low-grade myofibroblastic sarcoma show variable positivity for SMA and/or desmin. A subset show nuclear &beta;-catenin staining {17711447}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-02-11T10:18:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 406,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 239,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58570,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 239,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:24:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
